<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Details of Czech trade balance for January.</title>
<headline>Details of Czech trade balance for January.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is a breakdown of January trade figures for the Czech Republic as reported by the Czech Statistical Bureau (CSU) on Monday.</p>
<p>  (FOR JANUARY PERIOD)	  imports     exports     balance</p>
<p>BY TERRITORY (in billions of crowns)</p>
<p>Countries with a</p>
<p>  developed market economy     41.816	30.558     -13.597</p>
<p>   of that: EU countries	 36.808	28.191	-8.617</p>
<p>  Developing countries	    2.982	 2.256	-0.726</p>
<p>European countries with transitional economy, and</p>
<p>  CIS countries		    14.228	13.438	-0.790</p>
<p>Other countries with transitional or state</p>
<p>  economies			   0.987	 0.137	-0.850</p>
<p>  Unspecified countries	   0.029	 0.056	 0.027</p>
<p>  Total				60.042	46.445     -13.597</p>
<p>   of that: OECD countries     44.892	34.129     -10.763</p>
<p>BY PRODUCT GROUPS (in billions of crowns)</p>
<p>Agricultural products</p>
<p>  and foodstuffs		  4.843	   2.376    -2.467</p>
<p>Raw materials, unprocessed goods</p>
<p>  and chemical products	26.224	  20.837    -5.387</p>
<p>Machinery and</p>
<p>  transport equipment	  22.473	  16.702    -5.771</p>
<p>Industrial consumer</p>
<p>  products			  6.502	   6.530     0.028</p>
<p>  Total			    60.042	  46.445   -13.597</p>
<p>  Total index 1997/96 (pct) 108.2	    97.5</p>
<p>Note. All figures in billions of crowns on customs-cleared basis and subject to revision. Previously reported figures in brackets.</p>
<p>-- Alan Crosby, Prague Newsroom, 42-2-2423-0003</p>
</text>
